Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 01:45:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(compose): MainActivity overlay NavHost for
 History/Bookmarks (Phase D)

- New overlayNavHost ComposeView (activity_main.xml), wrapped alongside
  fragmentContainer in a FrameLayout so it can layer in the same bounds
  (LinearLayout can't overlap same-weight children) -- keeps toolbar
  visible above it, same visual as the old Fragment-in-fragmentContainer.
- Routes: EMPTY (common root, never rendered) / HISTORY / BOOKMARKS.
  openHistoryScreen()/openBookmarksScreen() now navigate+popUpTo(EMPTY)
  instead of a Fragment transaction.
- overlayNavHost's View visibility tracked via a
  NavController.OnDestinationChangedListener registered inside
  composition (DisposableEffect) -- not right after setContent(), since
  overlayNavController is a lateinit only assigned once the composable
  actually runs.
- System back pops the overlay's own stack first, before
  supportFragmentManager/Browser-back/bottom-nav checks.
- Old HistoryFragment.Callbacks/BookmarkFragment.Callbacks hand-off logic
  inlined directly into each route's onTap.
- Delete HistoryFragment.kt/BookmarkFragment.kt + retire the interface
  implementations on MainActivity. No fragment_history.xml/
  fragment_bookmarks.xml existed to delete (already ComposeView-only).
- Cross-reference grep: zero remaining code refs to either Fragment.

Not independently verified -- no local Android SDK/Gradle in this
environment; needs a CI build pass (Phase C's CI run caught two real
compile errors this same 'not verified' flag would've missed).

Updates COMPOSE_MIGRATION_V2-2.md: Phase D marked done, Order section
updated (E next).
